.th GRIPE I 4/22/75
.sh NAME
gripe \*- enter complaints and bug reports
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd gripe
[ option ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Gripe
is used to send a complaint to the gripe file.
.it Gripe
with no option sends the standard input to the gripe file
just like mail does.
The legal options are:
.ft I
.s3
.lp +8 7
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +8 7
s	send a complaint.
.s3
.lp +8 7
p	print the gripe file.
.s3
.lp +8 7
o	print the file of old gripes.
.s3
.lp +8 7
r	print the gripe reply file.
.i0
.dt
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 30
/usr/gripe/mailbox	the gripe file
/usr/gripe/mbox	the old gripe file
/bin/cat	to print files
/bin/mail	to update the files
.fi
.dt
.sh "SEE ALSO"
cat (I), mail (I)
.sh AUTHOR
Mike Tilson
.sh BUGS
Nothing wrong with the program, but no one is responsible
for reading or acting upon user complaints at the present time.
Users should read the complaints from  time to time to see
if they might feel like doing the work to fix the problems.
